+# Parity-even payload gate removal: inherited contract audit
+
+Conclusion: removing an even-coefficient pointwise payload ADD is valid for the bit supplier. The odd-prime address arithmetic remains unchanged. A new paid profile still requires the actual filtered word and full frame schedule; this conclusion alone does not certify a new kappa value.
+
+## Primary source evidence
+
+The bundled, unmodified primary section [`primary/03-motifs.tex`](primary/03-motifs.tex) states the following. Its exact source, attribution, and file hashes are recorded in [`primary/PROVENANCE.md`](primary/PROVENANCE.md).
+
+* Line50: in the bit construction scalars lie in F2.
+* Lines149–177: replace a scalar by an array in R^Omega, with R the scalar ring of the network. Common R-linear frames give the exact operator `D_out S_Omega D_in^-1`.
+* Around line223: the scalar domain need not equal the label field. Bit labels are rational subspaces even though the payload scalars are binary.
+* Lines483–493: rational-address frames are F2-linear permutations of array entries; the bit network uses pointwise XOR gates.
+
+The byte-pinned [`copied-centers-lemma.tex`](copied-centers-lemma.tex) in this package opens with its scalar restoration identity explicitly over F2. Its copy contract preserves the complete role stream, controls and spectators; each copy's frame change and erasure remain paid.
+
+The retained PR234 [`INTEGRATED_PROOF.md`](INTEGRATED_PROOF.md), line56, explicitly says: "The defining-integer lift need not equal the older supplier's decoder endpoint" and the majorant "uses neither signed integer restoration nor commutation between stage-dependent decoder channels." The package's signed integer decoder checks are stronger supplier evidence; the inherited bit interface does not impose their particular integer endpoint on a newly synthesized F2-equivalent word.
+
+The retained weighted bit theorem, [`three-stage-cover-bit.tex`](three-stage-cover-bit.tex), uses the odd-prime local ring Z/q^w for address fields and weighted address interchanges. Its rational projectors, unit-pivot tests, route matrices and fallback coefficients are address geometry. They are not the F2 payload ADD coefficients.
+
+## Operator proof
+
+Fix the finite complete address set Omega and let one stream be a vector in F2^Omega. A payload gate is `x_a <- x_a + (c mod2) x_b`. For even c this is the identity on every input, including arbitrary correlated dirty streams and spectators. Removing any number of these identity gates leaves the complete scalar operator S_Omega unchanged. Negative odd coefficients and coefficient3 also reduce to1, though the simplest experimental witness can retain their original signed integer representatives.
+
+Retain each original input/output frame and every remaining gate's original common frame. The common-frame identity then gives the same `D_out S_Omega D_in^-1` for the filtered word. In particular, every independent helper still has its required partial-swap residual and the existing completed-bank proof still applies. No integer identity of the new lift is needed to conclude this F2 operator identity.
+
+## Safe frame compression
+
+Deleting an ADD removes its operand-frame alignment requirement. For a given stream, collect successive MOVE operations between surviving uses. A use includes any surviving ADD, COPY read/write, ERASE or required phase/endpoint boundary. No use may be crossed merely because another stream is idle.
+
+Suppose the original local frames form a nested chain U0 <= U1 <= ... <= Uk. Their exact address changes telescope to `D_Uk D_U0^-1`. Their orthogonal increments are disjoint commuting projectors, so this is one allowed residual of rank dim(Uk)-dim(U0). In the reflected orientation the chain is the reversed complementary chain; the same endpoint difference and rank follow exactly. The ambient stage background cancels. Rebuild both ledgers from the actual surviving uses and actual basis inclusions; do not infer this from summed ranks alone.
+
+Keep every physical input/output family and its endpoint, all stage boundaries, all data routes/bridges, and every copied-center lifetime. For source527 the120 center copies in the five-stage construction have odd scatter coefficients, so parity filtering does not itself remove those episodes. The shared work stream cannot be used before COPY or after ERASE. A COPY is a barrier even if its original register has no intervening ADD.
+
+## Required finite admission
+
+1. Filter actual emitted ADD records by the literal coefficient modulo2; retain all odd-coefficient records in their original order. Check all20107 formal F2 source, target and dirty columns against the admitted shear. The expected local event counts before any further resynthesis are1,783,196 removed and786,621 retained.
+2. Generate the actual complemented inverse schedule, with fresh reverse copies as before, and verify every formal F2 column again. Do not reverse an erasure.
+3. Compute cancellation-free prefix bounds for the new literal signed forward/inverse projections. Recompute the five-stage bound and finite bill. Failure to reproduce the previous integer decoder is not itself a contract failure; a missing F2 dirty restoration is.
+4. Regenerate exact monotone forward/reflected physical paths and the complete paid histogram. Every fused residual's actual endpoints must be checked. Keep all remaining recursive children, copied-center calls, fallback allowance, data idle edges and stock.
+5. Rebind the completed banks and final global address lowering to the new word and tags. Their actual rational address projectors, odd-q routes and normalizers must not be reduced modulo2.
+6. Rerun actual basis/prime coverage, finite ordinary-leaf assembly, both rational moment engines and all47 outer inequalities before claiming a result.
+
+For simple monotone MOVE fusion the paid rank mass and physical stock remain unchanged; combining positive increments can improve the concave moment while reducing the number of children. Any different deficit or stock must be explained by a separate exact endpoint change. The displayed bound is still conditional on the retained all-size compiler, selectors, common ancestor charts, restored rows, routing, prime and analytic interfaces.
+
+Prepared with OpenAI Codex assistance. This audit is independent of the physical parity-filter/fusion implementation owned by the complex research lane.
